//! Frozen baseline of Bats suites under the scanned test directories that no
//! validate check invokes.
//!
//! `ExternalCheck::BatsSuiteRegistration` fails on any suite outside this list,
//! so the list is a ratchet: the count of orphaned suites can fall but never
//! rise. It is deliberately a plain list of paths rather than an in-place
//! `#[allow]`, because there is nothing in an unreferenced file to attach an
//! annotation to — the defect is the absence of a reference elsewhere.
//!
//! Measured on 25855847: 97 of the 144 suites under `tests/unit` and
//! `tests/lint` were invoked by nothing. Two of them are registered by the
//! change that introduced this file, leaving the 95 frozen below. Shrinking
//! this list by wiring a suite into the catalog is the intended direction of
//! travel; growing it is not, and requires deleting a line here by hand.
//!
//! This lives in its own module for a load-bearing reason: the check decides
//! "registered" by searching the text of the validation sources for the suite
//! path, so a baseline stored alongside that code would make every baselined
//! path look registered. The scanner skips this file by name.

